{
  "id": "6jzolj5",
  "title": "Chapter 15: Diseases and Immunity",
  "order": 64,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4b98635",
      "content": "Diseases are abnormal conditions that affect the normal functioning of the body. They may be caused by pathogens such as bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites, or due to nutritional deficiencies and lifestyle factors. The human immune system protects the body against disease-causing organisms."
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
