    {
      "id": "zeyepp4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Non‑Communicable Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kejroqv",
      "content": "• Diabetes – High blood sugar levels."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Vaccination introduces an antigen into the body to stimulate the production of antibodies and confer immunity against specific diseases.",
      "id": "bxnlguu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mhu95p5",
      "content": "• Hypertension – High blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m1042i2",
      "content": "• Cancer – Uncontrolled cell division."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h6ll4au",
      "content": "• Heart disease – Affects heart function."
    },
    {
