    {
      "id": "zirugzc",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Immune System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5ry8k4c",
      "content": "• The immune system protects the body from pathogens."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bv3r7mp",
      "content": "• It includes white blood cells, antibodies and lymphatic organs."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Innate Immunity",
        "Acquired Immunity"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Presence",
          "Present from birth",
          "Acquired after birth"
        ],
        [
          "Specificity",
          "Non-specific defense mechanism",
          "Pathogen-specific response"
        ],
        [
          "Memory",
          "Lacks immunological memory",
          "Retains memory for faster secondary response"
        ],
        [
          "Components",
          "Physical & chemical barriers (skin, mucosa)",
          "T-cells, B-cells, and specific antibodies"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "7orosz7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ag4p1ke",
      "content": "• It identifies and destroys harmful microorganisms."
    },
    {
      "id": "khv19l5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Types of Immunity"
    },
    {
