    {
      "id": "ww0opy1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Vaccination"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "li7sp11",
      "content": "• Vaccines stimulate the immune system to produce antibodies."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xqylgtg",
      "content": "• They protect against diseases such as polio, measles and hepatitis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "sc76eio",
      "content": "• Vaccination is one of the most effective methods of disease prevention."
    },
    {
      "id": "5por9rf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Prevention of Diseases"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ha51x6t",
      "content": "• Maintain personal hygiene."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "08dgb02",
      "content": "• Eat a balanced diet."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dvbb2y1",
      "content": "• Drink clean water."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Edward Jenner is known as the 'Father of Vaccination' for developing the smallpox vaccine in 1796.",
        "Key deficiency diseases frequently asked: Vitamin A (Night Blindness), Vitamin C (Scurvy), Vitamin D (Rickets), and Iodine (Goitre).",
        "Distinguish between Active Immunity (body produces own antibodies) and Passive Immunity (direct transfer of readymade antibodies)."
      ],
      "id": "umzpmd8"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1lrcwsl",
      "content": "• Regular vaccination."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x3ll3hs",
      "content": "• Control insects and mosquitoes."
    },
    {
      "id": "01cc4yp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "02ipv84",
      "content": "• Vaccines help build immunity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ih4pccj",
      "content": "• Vitamin deficiencies cause several diseases."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "100xd2f",
      "content": "• Pathogens include bacteria, viruses, fungi and parasites."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rmk787u",
      "content": "• The immune system defends the body against infections."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
